{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "זרע זרוע אשר יזרע טהור הוא", :translit "zer'a zeru'a asher yizzare'a tahor hu", :gloss "seed sown that is sown, it is pure"} {:he "זרעים שזרען טהורות", :translit "zera'im she-zar'an tehorot", :gloss "seeds whose planting is pure"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "זרע זרוע אשר יזרע טהור הוא", :b "זרעים שזרען טהורות"}], :frame {:text "Leviticus 11:37 states that seed grain which is sown remains pure even if a carcass fell on it, as long as it was not moistened with water. The verse itself pronounces 'טהור הוא' — it is pure — and Ba'al HaTurim reads the phrase as encoding a compressed summary of the law's substance: the category of plantings (זרעים) is not rendered impure by contact with an animal carcass.", :sources ["Leviticus 11:37"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "זרע זרוע אשר יזרע טהור הוא", :a-value 1580, :b "זרעים שזרען טהורות", :b-value 1580, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:22:57.609415300Z", :model "glm-5.2"}